464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Eternity is beyond the scope of our understanding, so it is futile attempting to explain it. Eternity has no beginning but time does. It was at a point along the unveiling of eternity that God decided to create time. In Gen 1:14, God commanded lights to appear in the sky and to separate day from night and to show the time for seasons, special days, and years \(CEV\). Thus, time was created on earth and all earthly creatures including man were subject to time. Time is a drop in the ocean of eternity. Imagine a tadpole put in a closed cup, with all the food it needs throughout its short lifespan, and the cup then thrown into an ocean. Asking that tadpole to explain the length, breath, depth, dynamics, physics and chemistry of the ocean is a simpler task than a man within time trying to wrap his mind around explaining eternity and )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
