468 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Any measurable time, no matter how large is a grain in the sand dune of eternity. So, a billion or a zillion years is still nothing in the context of eternity. The human mind cannot fathom or explain the Eternal God. This is the reason the Bible says, only fools say in their hearts "There is no God." . . . The Lord looks down from heaven on the entire human race; He looks to see if anyone is truly wise, if anyone seeks God \(Psa.14:1-2\). It truly takes a fool to conclude that God does not exist because he cannot explain Him within his limited frame of mind and time. God looks down from the realm of eternity into time to see if there is anyone who is wise enough to know that He exists beyond time and cannot be completely described or subjected within the frame of time.)
/E (Any measurable time, no matter how large is a grain in the sand dune of eternity. So, a billion or a zillion years is still nothing in the context of eternity. The human mind cannot fathom or explain the Eternal God. This is the reason the Bible says, only fools say in their hearts "There is no God." . . . The Lord looks down from heaven on the entire human race; He looks to see if anyone is truly wise, if anyone seeks God \(Psa.14:1-2\). It truly takes a fool to conclude that God does not exist because he cannot explain Him within his limited frame of mind and time. God looks down from the realm of eternity into time to see if there is anyone who is wise enough to know that He exists beyond time and cannot be completely described or subjected within the frame of time.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
