473 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Monday or Tuesday, January or December but just one long stretch of time. Imagine you are born, go to school, work, marry, die and do everything on earth within a long continuum of a day without the seasonal coming of night and day, a week after another, month after month or year after year. How would life be? How do you measure progress? How do you rest?)
/E (Monday or Tuesday, January or December but just one long stretch of time. Imagine you are born, go to school, work, marry, die and do everything on earth within a long continuum of a day without the seasonal coming of night and day, a week after another, month after month or year after year. How would life be? How do you measure progress? How do you rest?)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
474 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Every day, week, month, and year is organized into seasons for the purpose of order. Day time and night time are seasons of the day. Morning, Afternoon, Evening and Night are  seasons within the day. Each day is a season within a week. Each week is a new season within the month. Every New Year is a new season. A year also has different climatic seasons depending on the part of the world. Temperate regions have Autumn, Spring, Winter and Fall. Tropical regions have Rainy Season, Dry Season, and Harmattan. Farm-life has planting seasons, growing seasons, harvest seasons. Each Decade and Millennium is the introduction of a new season.  Even events in life usher new seasons - graduating out of school, getting married, giving birth to children starting a business or career all usher us into new seasons. A new political government brings a state or territory into a new season and so many other examples that depict change in seasons.)
/E (Every day, week, month, and year is organized into seasons for the purpose of order. Day time and night time are seasons of the day. Morning, Afternoon, Evening and Night are  seasons within the day. Each day is a season within a week. Each week is a new season within the month. Every New Year is a new season. A year also has different climatic seasons depending on the part of the world. Temperate regions have Autumn, Spring, Winter and Fall. Tropical regions have Rainy Season, Dry Season, and Harmattan. Farm-life has planting seasons, growing seasons, harvest seasons. Each Decade and Millennium is the introduction of a new season.  Even events in life usher new seasons - graduating out of school, getting married, giving birth to children starting a business or career all usher us into new seasons. A new political government brings a state or territory into a new season and so many other examples that depict change in seasons.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
475 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The power of seasons lies in the fact that each new season always brings a new hope, opportunity and possibility. Each day we wake with a renewed hope to achieve what we could not the day before. If life on earth was not programmed to be in daily seasons, one major negative effect would be hopelessness and exhaustion. Life would be a too long and tiring journey to the grave. One purpose of seasons is to renew hope; the hope of change, the hope of possibility, the hope of a fresh start and the hope of newness. )
/E (The power of seasons lies in the fact that each new season always brings a new hope, opportunity and possibility. Each day we wake with a renewed hope to achieve what we could not the day before. If life on earth was not programmed to be in daily seasons, one major negative effect would be hopelessness and exhaustion. Life would be a too long and tiring journey to the grave. One purpose of seasons is to renew hope; the hope of change, the hope of possibility, the hope of a fresh start and the hope of newness. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
