<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (A scriptural example of the understanding of what to do at each time of life is shown in Gen. 49: 27. It says, "Benjamin is a ravenous wolf; in the morning he shall devour the prey, and at night he shall divide the spoil." Benjamin, like a wolf, understands that the morning is for hunting prey and evening is for eating the meat. Lack of wisdom makes some people to eat all the meat in the morning so they have nothing to eat at night. This is the reason some have to still be hunting when they should be resting. )
