/T (Just as the day, life could be partitioned into the morning, afternoon, evening and night. Knowing what to do at every time of life is the secret to greatness in life. The Bible uses the analogy of the day to portray human lifetime, it says, for you, a thousand years are as a passing day, as brief as a few night hours. You sweep people away like dreams that disappear. They are like grass that springs up in the morning. In the morning it blooms and flourishes, but by evening it is dry and withered \(Psa. 90:4 - 6\). Figuratively, people are born and they spring in the morning, grow in the noon, become dry in the evening, and wither and die at night. )
