/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Prov. 22:6 says, train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it. Childhood is the earliest stage of the morning of life - the dawn of life. This is the time for training. It is important to ingrain sound doctrine, character, godliness, responsibility, and principles strongly into children between the ages of zero to twelve; else, the entire subsequent efforts would be remedial measures. However, people in their teens are to be exposed to responsibility. A wise man once said, the concept of adolescent is being used to excuse foolishness in many people. The truth about life is that you are either a child or an adult, and you become an adult when you are no longer a child.  1 Cor. 13:11-12 says, when I was a child, I spoke and thought and reasoned as a child. But when I grew up, I put away childish things. Thus, according to scriptures, you stop being a child when you grow up. Some grow up in their teens, some in their twenties, some in their forties, some never grow up. )
/E (Prov. 22:6 says, train up a child in the way he should go: and when he is old, he will not depart from it. Childhood is the earliest stage of the morning of life - the dawn of life. This is the time for training. It is important to ingrain sound doctrine, character, godliness, responsibility, and principles strongly into children between the ages of zero to twelve; else, the entire subsequent efforts would be remedial measures. However, people in their teens are to be exposed to responsibility. A wise man once said, the concept of adolescent is being used to excuse foolishness in many people. The truth about life is that you are either a child or an adult, and you become an adult when you are no longer a child.  1 Cor. 13:11-12 says, when I was a child, I spoke and thought and reasoned as a child. But when I grew up, I put away childish things. Thus, according to scriptures, you stop being a child when you grow up. Some grow up in their teens, some in their twenties, some in their forties, some never grow up. )
