/S /H2
/T (1.    Seek and Know God: Ps. 63:1 says O God, thou art my God; early will I seek thee: my soul thirstiest for thee, my flesh longest for thee in a dry and thirsty land, where no water is. Isa. 55:6 says, seek ye the Lord while he may be found, call ye upon him while he is near. This suggests that a time comes when it is more difficult to seek God if you have not done so earlier.)
/E (1.    Seek and Know God: Ps. 63:1 says O God, thou art my God; early will I seek thee: my soul thirstiest for thee, my flesh longest for thee in a dry and thirsty land, where no water is. Isa. 55:6 says, seek ye the Lord while he may be found, call ye upon him while he is near. This suggests that a time comes when it is more difficult to seek God if you have not done so earlier.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
