<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (On a regular day, when you see someone sleeping in the afternoon, they are either lazy or sick - except they worked night shifts. However, the noon comes before the night in life so the one who sleeps in the noon of life is not because he worked a night shift but because he is planning to work a night shift. If you do not want to be working when you should be resting and mentoring others, you should work in the noon. )
/E (On a regular day, when you see someone sleeping in the afternoon, they are either lazy or sick - except they worked night shifts. However, the noon comes before the night in life so the one who sleeps in the noon of life is not because he worked a night shift but because he is planning to work a night shift. If you do not want to be working when you should be resting and mentoring others, you should work in the noon. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
562 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (This is the time when your life work must be full-fledged. Jesus said I must work the works of him that sent me, while it is day: the night cometh, when no man can work \(John 9:4\). You should pursue life with such urgency at the noon like that is all you have to fulfill your destiny, purpose and goals. After the noon, diminishing returns may overtake your physical strength and you may have to go at an easier pace in life. So, run in your youth - the morning and the noon. According to Lam.3:27, it is good for a man that he bear the yoke in his youth.)
/E (This is the time when your life work must be full-fledged. Jesus said I must work the works of him that sent me, while it is day: the night cometh, when no man can work \(John 9:4\). You should pursue life with such urgency at the noon like that is all you have to fulfill your destiny, purpose and goals. After the noon, diminishing returns may overtake your physical strength and you may have to go at an easier pace in life. So, run in your youth - the morning and the noon. According to Lam.3:27, it is good for a man that he bear the yoke in his youth.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
