566 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (1.    Take responsibility and become self-dependent: While a large part of the morning is spent as being dependent on parents and guardian, one should have learned self-reliance in the late morning of life and become self-dependent in the noon. The noon is not the time to be feeding on parents, friends and relatives. It is a time when your hands should be sufficient for you. Deut. 33:7 shows the blessing of Judah: saying, Hear, Lord, the voice of Judah, and bring him unto his people: let his hands be sufficient for him; and be thou a help to him from his enemies. By the time you get to the noon of life, your hands must be sufficient for you and you should not be dependent on someone. )
/E (1.    Take responsibility and become self-dependent: While a large part of the morning is spent as being dependent on parents and guardian, one should have learned self-reliance in the late morning of life and become self-dependent in the noon. The noon is not the time to be feeding on parents, friends and relatives. It is a time when your hands should be sufficient for you. Deut. 33:7 shows the blessing of Judah: saying, Hear, Lord, the voice of Judah, and bring him unto his people: let his hands be sufficient for him; and be thou a help to him from his enemies. By the time you get to the noon of life, your hands must be sufficient for you and you should not be dependent on someone. )
