580 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (When you see people in their fifties, sixties and seventies still gallivanting and rocking life as if they are still young - partying, carousing with the girls and boys, and riding life in funfair, you have met a great fool. No matter the achievement such people had in their morning and nights, they are not planning for tomorrow. )
/E (When you see people in their fifties, sixties and seventies still gallivanting and rocking life as if they are still young - partying, carousing with the girls and boys, and riding life in funfair, you have met a great fool. No matter the achievement such people had in their morning and nights, they are not planning for tomorrow. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
581 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (There is a tomorrow in the time of life; your tomorrow is your next generation - your children, legacy, and the future of what you have spent your life building. When you see people in their fifties, sixties and seventies retiring into a life of laxity, you have met an average person. What to do in the evening is to build the next generation and transfer the baton to them. Spend your noon raising and building people as you also build structures. Spend the evening of your life, pouring all the wealth of your wisdom and experience into the next generation and make sure you transfer all your vision, wisdom, and systems into the hands of younger people you have raised so that when night comes and you go to sleep, you can be rest assured that what you spent your entire life on will outlive you. )
/E (There is a tomorrow in the time of life; your tomorrow is your next generation - your children, legacy, and the future of what you have spent your life building. When you see people in their fifties, sixties and seventies retiring into a life of laxity, you have met an average person. What to do in the evening is to build the next generation and transfer the baton to them. Spend your noon raising and building people as you also build structures. Spend the evening of your life, pouring all the wealth of your wisdom and experience into the next generation and make sure you transfer all your vision, wisdom, and systems into the hands of younger people you have raised so that when night comes and you go to sleep, you can be rest assured that what you spent your entire life on will outlive you. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
582 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (It is vanity to spend all your life building something that dies when you die because, in a little while, the story of such a person would sound the same with that of someone who never built. Every worthwhile vision you have must stretch beyond your lifetime even from inception. In other words, you must factor how every vision you have now would thrive and grow after you are gone. As you build your God-given vision, you must build the system to be able to eventually do without you. Identify potential successors from the noon of your life, build them along as you build the vision, invest in the people and make them wiser, better and mightier than you. )
/E (It is vanity to spend all your life building something that dies when you die because, in a little while, the story of such a person would sound the same with that of someone who never built. Every worthwhile vision you have must stretch beyond your lifetime even from inception. In other words, you must factor how every vision you have now would thrive and grow after you are gone. As you build your God-given vision, you must build the system to be able to eventually do without you. Identify potential successors from the noon of your life, build them along as you build the vision, invest in the people and make them wiser, better and mightier than you. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
