/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Generally, in life, the end is superior to the means. In fact, the end determines if the means is worthwhile or not. The end talks about what one is trying to achieve, the means describes how one goes about achieving it. If the means outweighs the end, purpose has been defeated. Therefore, means may change even when the end is fixed.  )
/E (Generally, in life, the end is superior to the means. In fact, the end determines if the means is worthwhile or not. The end talks about what one is trying to achieve, the means describes how one goes about achieving it. If the means outweighs the end, purpose has been defeated. Therefore, means may change even when the end is fixed.  )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [2]
>>
