635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (2.   The Power of Intuition: This is the cognitive ability of man to know beyond what he sees, hears, or receives from his physical senses in the natural. Intuition is an inner knowing and perception that makes a man to pick certain knowledge without natural agencies of communication. Man through intuition is supposed to know that God as God and know His purposes and course for his live. The fundamental things to be known about God and life is placed in man by intuition so that no one would be with excuse \(Rom1: 19 -20\). Adam knew everything intuitively before the fall but human intuition became dull by the Fall, and it is now only sharpened by correct spiritual partnerships. )
/E (2.   The Power of Intuition: This is the cognitive ability of man to know beyond what he sees, hears, or receives from his physical senses in the natural. Intuition is an inner knowing and perception that makes a man to pick certain knowledge without natural agencies of communication. Man through intuition is supposed to know that God as God and know His purposes and course for his live. The fundamental things to be known about God and life is placed in man by intuition so that no one would be with excuse \(Rom1: 19 -20\). Adam knew everything intuitively before the fall but human intuition became dull by the Fall, and it is now only sharpened by correct spiritual partnerships. )
