642 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Man's Power of Choice )
/E (Man's Power of Choice )
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
643 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In view of the God-given powers deposited in man as explained, it is obvious that it would be impossible for God to run the world of men by absolute predestination without violating man. So, predestination is real but it is not absolute.  Choice is the power of man to exercise his will in any direction he desires and self-determine his outcome in life. Eph. 1:4 - 5 says, just as God chose us in Him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blame before Him in love, having predestined us to adoption as sons by Jesus Christ to Himself, according to the good pleasure of His will. God predestines a fixed end for the bigger picture that He is working out in every context but the fulfillment in individual lives is neither automatic nor fixed but dependent on individual choices. For example, God predestined salvation for all men but people die daily without being saved - their choice. However, the predestined end will still be achieved. So, God speaks, I have sworn by my own name; I have spoken the truth, and I will never go back on my word: Every knee will bend to me, and every tongue will confess allegiance to me. \(Isa 45:23 NLT\) Everyone will eventually bow to the Lordship of Jesus but the place they will be by the time they do is based on their choice. It is better to release your choice right now and bow to His Lordship in this lifetime.  God will achieve whatever He wants to, no matter how long it will take and how many people He will have to pass over until He gets a willing fit for each operation in the algorithm of the codes that needs to be in place for His program to run. He will even create another person for the specific purpose if at all there is no one among the billions on earth exercising their choices in the direction he wants. )
/E (In view of the God-given powers deposited in man as explained, it is obvious that it would be impossible for God to run the world of men by absolute predestination without violating man. So, predestination is real but it is not absolute.  Choice is the power of man to exercise his will in any direction he desires and self-determine his outcome in life. Eph. 1:4 - 5 says, just as God chose us in Him before the foundation of the world, that we should be holy and without blame before Him in love, having predestined us to adoption as sons by Jesus Christ to Himself, according to the good pleasure of His will. God predestines a fixed end for the bigger picture that He is working out in every context but the fulfillment in individual lives is neither automatic nor fixed but dependent on individual choices. For example, God predestined salvation for all men but people die daily without being saved - their choice. However, the predestined end will still be achieved. So, God speaks, I have sworn by my own name; I have spoken the truth, and I will never go back on my word: Every knee will bend to me, and every tongue will confess allegiance to me. \(Isa 45:23 NLT\) Everyone will eventually bow to the Lordship of Jesus but the place they will be by the time they do is based on their choice. It is better to release your choice right now and bow to His Lordship in this lifetime.  God will achieve whatever He wants to, no matter how long it will take and how many people He will have to pass over until He gets a willing fit for each operation in the algorithm of the codes that needs to be in place for His program to run. He will even create another person for the specific purpose if at all there is no one among the billions on earth exercising their choices in the direction he wants. )
/Pg 51 0 R
/K [1]
>>
