746 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (There is something as due season in life. Ps. 1:3 says, and he shall be like a tree planted by the rivers of water, that bringeth forth his fruit in his season; his leaf also shall not wither; and whatsoever he doeth shall prosper.)
/Pg 75 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
747 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (There is a due season for everything in life. When the time you should have had a result is passed and it is not forthcoming, it should become an issue of concern. Delay, belated life and denial are satanic strategies for causing failure in life. If time is going and the milestones are not coming, then such life is running behind schedule and unless there is divine intervention, failure or short-changing of destiny is imminent. We should demand for the fruits of our life in due season. When it is time to get a thing in life, then it must be demanded from life.  )
/Pg 75 0 R
/K [2]
>>
